1:0-93 "/// `entry` files (SPEC §4.3): the entries of a table or a keyed list spread over files, one" comment.line.documentation.canon
2:0-94 "/// entry per file or several. `@files` says where a new entry's file goes. Entry order is the" comment.line.documentation.canon
3:0-91 "/// literal's entries, then the entry files in path order, then source order inside a file." comment.line.documentation.canon
4:0-95 "/// Keys are unique across the literal and every entry file: a duplicate is `E3101` for a table" comment.line.documentation.canon
5:0-98 "/// and `E3102` for a keyed list (TYPES §9.3), and an edit that would make one is `ErrKeyExists`." comment.line.documentation.canon
6:0-68 "/// The examples stay free of errors, so no file here repeats a key." comment.line.documentation.canon
